  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      This isn't really a "which is cheaper" comparison, it's a "what do you actually need" one. <strong>ByteSIM</strong> sells real local phone numbers, calls and texts included, in a handful of countries, at a higher price and with an ID-verification step. <strong>RedteaGO</strong> sells data and nothing else by default, at some of the lowest starting prices on this site, with calls and texts only on plans specifically labeled for it. Pick ByteSIM if a working local number matters to your trip. Pick RedteaGO if all you want is cheap data.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Core Difference: A Real Phone Number vs. Data-Only by Default</h2>
  <p>
    ByteSIM is unusual among the cheap data-only eSIM apps on this site because it also sells real local phone numbers, with calls, texts, hotspot sharing, and a local IP address, in select countries including the US, Canada, UK, France, Spain, Australia, Vietnam, South Korea, and Thailand. We bought one ourselves: ByteSIM's Spain "Mega Plan with Unlimited Calls & EU Roaming," which came with 100GB of Spain data, 15GB of EU roaming data, unlimited calls within Spain, 500 minutes of EU roaming calls, and a real <strong>+34 Spanish phone number</strong>, for 27 days. Getting that number required uploading a passport photo and a selfie for ID verification, which ByteSIM's own site says applies only to local-number plans, not its regular data-only travel eSIMs.
  </p>
  <p>
    RedteaGO's own FAQ says plainly that call and text service is "only available in certain regions," on plans marked with a separate "Calls/Texts Available" label, plus a distinct Call & Text eSIM package sold apart from the regular data plans. Most RedteaGO plans are data-only. If a working phone number is part of what you're buying, RedteaGO isn't the default answer the way ByteSIM's number plans are; you'd need to specifically find a labeled plan or the separate Call & Text package.
  </p>

